{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire","id":615841,"title":"Exhausting a Vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-04T18:06:13-07:00","id":615841,"title":"Exhausting a Vampire?","content":"Several of the new rituals in an upcoming book require the vampire to dance till exhaustion. How long does that take?<br /> What are the game effects of a vamp being exhausted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T20:47:46-07:00","id":615959,"title":"","content":"I thought that was addressed. Which book and rituals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T22:24:48-07:00","id":616006,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Covenants, the Circle of the Crone development blog. It has a bunch of rituals in it that are ritualistic dances that do stuff like boost your Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T23:00:28-07:00","id":616023,"title":"","content":"The latest version doesn't say dance until exhausted. You dance until the ritual is complete at which point you are exhausted. You spend a willpower point to recover. I guess the effect is you need to spend a point of willpower. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Vampires and exhaustion is a sketchy thing. They never seem to actually get exhausted, but they have limitations based on exhaustion. Narrative explanation, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T23:11:12-07:00","id":616027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=616023#post616023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latest version doesn't say dance until exhausted. You dance until the ritual is complete at which point you are exhausted. You spend a willpower point to recover. I guess the effect is you need to spend a point of willpower. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Vampires and exhaustion is a sketchy thing. They never seem to actually get exhausted, but they have limitations based on exhaustion. Narrative explanation, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mental/spiritual/Beast-related exhaustion versus physical exhaustion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T23:43:30-07:00","id":616034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=616027#post616027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mental/spiritual/Beast-related exhaustion versus physical exhaustion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is a distinction in the end, but your version sounds better so let's go with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: I'm referring to a distinction between our questions, not physical and mental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 08-06-2015, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:01:10-07:00","id":616316,"title":"","content":"To me, it's the ritual causing a mystical or mental exhaustion. Dead bodies do not get physically tired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:29:57-07:00","id":616338,"title":"","content":"I think Chris once explained that vampires <i>do</i> get tired when they exert themselves just like anyone else of their stamina level. It's a bit of a glitch in their &quot;emulate the living&quot; package. Then once they've rested a bit their body suddenly remembers it's undead and they snap back to full power. Which I would run as being just fine the next scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T07:17:33-07:00","id":616425,"title":"","content":"I get exhausted after putting all the paperwork through for work. The mind needs as much of a chance to recover as the body does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T07:57:58-07:00","id":616473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire#post615841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several of the new rituals in an upcoming book require the vampire to dance till exhaustion. How long does that take?</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes however many turns the player requires to roll the necessary successes for the extended action of performing the ritual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire#post615841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the game effects of a vamp being exhausted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Loss of a willpower point or vitae point, depending on the ritual.<br /> <br /> This is one of those mechanic vs. narrative semantic issues. Players track their character's mental and mystical energy as willpower and vitae points respectively, but the characters themselves don't track their energy that way. Instead, a character would intuitively sense that they had expended some amount of personal energy from a finite reserve. They would describe this as feeling &quot;drained&quot; to some degree, and this is what the term &quot;exhaustion&quot; means in this context. So, the mechanic of &quot;roll successes and spend willpower/vitae&quot; becomes the narrative of &quot;dance until exhaustion&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:01:48-07:00","id":616548,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking about this earlier.<br /> <br /> I figure it's a physical limitations thing vs a conscious/mental thing (of course, I project my belief that there isn't a mind/body distinction into the game about vampires with primeval hunger monsters living in their souls, so...). Basically, a vampiric body has specific physical limitations just like any other body, and whether or not the vampire is <i>tired</i> is irrelevant: their muscles still experience microtears and Vitae still has to circulate the magical animus through their body at a finite rate.<br /> <br /> After getting to that point in Order of the Stick where Roy climbs a mountain in the afterlife for 3 months and doesn't realize it, I really enjoy using mundane, simple explanations for what people might think are odd or exceptional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:05:27-07:00","id":616551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=616425#post616425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get exhausted after putting all the paperwork through for work. The mind needs as much of a chance to recover as the body does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it weird that I keep trying to figure out mechanics to represent this? Like, do you have to spend a willpower point to complete paperwork, or does paperwork afflict you with the &quot;Bureaucratic Lethargy&quot; condition? Would coffee provide an equipment bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:31:23-07:00","id":616580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=616548#post616548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking about this earlier.<br /> <br /> I figure it's a physical limitations thing vs a conscious/mental thing</div> </div> </div> </div>Cut to a dojo where in an elder Mekhet is attempting to train his childe in the combat applications of celerity.<ul><li>NEONATE: [Panting, on his hands and knees]</li> <li>ELDER: How did I beat you?</li> <li>NEONATE: You [pant] You're too fast.</li> <li>ELDER: Do you think my being faster and stronger has anything to do with my muscles now that I'm dead?</li> <li>NEONATE: [unable to catch his breath]</li> <li>ELDER: [leans forward] Do you think you're actually breathing that air?</li> <li>NEONATE: [squints at him and then steadily rises to his feet]</li> <li>ELDER: [turns away] Again!</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","user":"Vyrkolash","date":". 08-05-2015, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T10:57:42-07:00","id":616671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=616551#post616551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it weird that I keep trying to figure out mechanics to represent this? Like, do you have to spend a willpower point to complete paperwork, or does paperwork afflict you with the &quot;Bureaucratic Lethargy&quot; condition? Would coffee provide an equipment bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div> Extended and contested social maneuvering system, and when the paper work wins, I get the Fugue Condition. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T16:15:40-07:00","id":616871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=616338#post616338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Chris once explained that vampires <i>do</i> get tired when they exert themselves just like anyone else of their stamina level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose said the same. She never offered an explanation, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T05:50:39-07:00","id":617641,"title":"","content":"I think it probably depends on the context. I'm not sure exhaustion is always covered for mortals either. If it was dance until exhausted and mortals could work the ritual, I would be just as lost. There are certain aspects that are covered, but they don't always apply to vampires. You can't get out of breath when you don't need to breathe. Hunger is not based on any biological function for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T06:09:18-07:00","id":617675,"title":"","content":"Hunger is just about the closest thing they have to a normal metabolic process. All the other stuff is debatable, but sooner or later they <i>do</i> need to eat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T06:50:06-07:00","id":617712,"title":"","content":"They definitely get hungry. It just doesn't have anything to do with blood glucose, digestive tract contents, or any of the other reasons a person feels hungry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T07:18:36-07:00","id":617733,"title":"","content":"Vitae is more or less magic blood glucose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T08:27:41-07:00","id":617786,"title":"","content":"Right. So magic that makes someone hungry works on a vampire, but when a vampire is affected by insulin they should not get hungry. If there was a rule that said a character can run for a number of hours equal to Stamina + Resolve after which they begin taking a point of bashing damage for every hour of continued running then vampires follow the rule too. If there was a rule that said 10 minutes of sprinting results in the Exhausted condition then vampires follow the rule, at least as much as such a condition might affect a walking, talking corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T09:13:33-07:00","id":617817,"title":"","content":"Vampires feel physical fatigue when they exert themselves. However, it's not accompanied by the biological factors that make recovery hard for a human. They just get a bit tired from keeping the muscles working*, then recover quickly. Say by the next scene or after a few minutes with less exertion.<br /> <br /> * Think of this as the low-key version of Physical Intensity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-06-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T13:09:11-07:00","id":618000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=617817#post617817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires feel physical fatigue when they exert themselves. However, it's not accompanied by the biological factors that make recovery hard for a human. They just get a bit tired from keeping the muscles working*, then recover quickly. Say by the next scene or after a few minutes with less exertion.<br /> <br /> * Think of this as the low-key version of Physical Intensity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just so we're clear; there's no mechanic in the rules expressing this, just as there is no mechanic for expressing a mortal feeling fatigued after they ran for a mile. It's purely a narrative thing right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T14:17:21-07:00","id":618073,"title":"","content":"It means their stamina stat means something. If they never got tired it would effectively be infinite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T06:42:28-07:00","id":618768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=618000#post618000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just so we're clear; there's no mechanic in the rules expressing this, just as there is no mechanic for expressing a mortal feeling fatigued after they ran for a mile. It's purely a narrative thing right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have reread the blue book. I'm sure you can hack something if there isn't. loss of will power could be a measure of mental alertness and fatigue.<br /> Problem is vamps don't recover willpower from daysleep anymore.<br /> <br /> This becomes important if read some other threads like the current Vamp vs Werewolf thread. A viable tactic by either side is wearing the other side down.<br /> Making your opponent tired and not letting him recover so he starts making stupid mistakes. Thats how vamp should take out a teams of hunters . Hit &amp; run tactics.<br /> Using influence so they are hassled during the day and night. Never letting them rest.<br /> <br /> So having a system to track this is necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T16:37:10-07:00","id":620710,"title":"","content":"Wait. Vamps don't recover willpower from daysleep? Where is that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:25:38-07:00","id":620937,"title":"","content":"It doesn't explicitly say. It just doesn't mention it being an option for vampires. <br /> <br /> It doesn't mention it being an option for mortals either. The only time it ever comes up at all is when it mentions that <i>strix</i> don't get any because they don't sleep. <br /> <br /> So, since vampires <i>do</i> sleep, it's safe to assume that they are intended to regain willpower from doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T04:54:53-07:00","id":621086,"title":"","content":"I think it was said in the preview stage. Mortals could be an oversight, but I'm sure they would have put it in for vampires if they intended for them to recover willpower from daysleep. However, they might have backtracked a bit to put it up in the air too. I don't think it will really hurt to give willpower for sleep. Consider it an optional rule. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T07:49:14-07:00","id":621253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=617817#post617817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires feel physical fatigue when they exert themselves. However, it's not accompanied by the biological factors that make recovery hard for a human. They just get a bit tired from keeping the muscles working*, then recover quickly. Say by the next scene or after a few minutes with less exertion.<br /> <br /> * Think of this as the low-key version of Physical Intensity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Presumably this means a vampire with Resilience 5 (+5 to stamina) will take a long time to get fatigued?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:27:36-07:00","id":621317,"title":"","content":"Yes. Superhuman stamina does tend to come with stamina that is somewhat superior to human levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T09:22:22-07:00","id":621397,"title":"","content":"Short term fatigue has never really had any rules, only long term. And, in the latter case, its a Stamina + Resolve roll. So, if you have resilience 5, you'd be going a long time with that super Stamina score of yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T10:24:41-07:00","id":621443,"title":"","content":"For a ghoul. Vampires don't really need to sleep, so I don't think fatigue would ever apply. The short term stuff is actually damage to the body like muscle tears. If there were rules to cover it then vampires would follow those rules. So they say vampires suffer from exhaustion. Outside of multiple scenes with no downtime in between, exhaustion doesn't tend to come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T19:40:29-07:00","id":621803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=621443#post621443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a ghoul. Vampires don't really need to sleep, so I don't think fatigue would ever apply. The short term stuff is actually damage to the body like muscle tears. If there were rules to cover it then vampires would follow those rules. So they say vampires suffer from exhaustion. Outside of multiple scenes with no downtime in between, exhaustion doesn't tend to come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I thought I read it it somewhere in Blood and Smoke, or something previewing it, about daysleep no longer giving willpower back.<br /> 2 On the subject of Vampires not needed sleep;<br /> A. Nos have True Worm merit that lets them stay awake if they are deep enough underground.<br /> B. Several of the new disciplines levels require daysleep to activate or set up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T20:18:01-07:00","id":621846,"title":"","content":"Vampires can sort of sleep, but they don't <i>need</i> to sleep. They don't pass out under the same circumstances that a mortal would. A vampire's version of sleep is more like a coma for mortals. The fatigue rule is about staying awake and then what happens until you sleep or pass out. Vampires have their daysleep rules which would take the place of the fatigue rules. If a vampire makes it through the day without sleeping then they are wide awake when night comes. The &quot;need&quot; for a vampire to sleep during the day is supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T02:18:55-07:00","id":621979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=621846#post621846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a vampire makes it through the day without sleeping then they are wide awake when night comes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they aren't. The resolution for the fatigued condition is a full day's sleep. Also it speaks of a cumulative 1 die penalty that goes up every 6 hours. If the condition reset at night it would almost never get a chance to increase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T03:02:16-07:00","id":621995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/615841-exhausting-a-vampire?p=621979#post621979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they aren't. The resolution for the fatigued condition is a full day's sleep. Also it speaks of a cumulative 1 die penalty that goes up every 6 hours. If the condition reset at night it would almost never get a chance to increase.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean Lethargic, you can roll well and not get the condition. Fatigue is different. You go 24 hours and then it is a test to see how long until you drop. You still have to sleep sometime. A vampire that rolls well might never need to and Dragons are in an even better position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}